# Multi-Scale Token System (MTS)

Adaptive resolution processing for vision-language models with text-guided supervision.

## Modified Files

### Core Processing
- `custom_models/qwen2_5_vl/multiscale_processor.py`
  - `MultiScaleTokenProcessor`: Main processor with text-guided visual projection
  - `TextGuidedVisualProjector`: CLIP-based text-visual alignment
  - Confidence mask generation from bounding boxes
  - Auxiliary BCE loss for training

- `custom_models/qwen2_5_vl/multiscale_image_processor.py`
  - Multi-scale image preprocessing
  - Tracks original image size and resize ratios

### Model Integration
- `custom_models/qwen2_5_vl/modeling_qwen2_5_vl.py`
  - Passes `text_prompt`, `bbox_scale_xy`, `instruction` through forward chain
  - Combines MTS auxiliary loss with main loss

### Data & Training
- `src/llamafactory/data/collator.py`
  - Extracts `instruction` from input_ids
  - Computes `bbox_scale_xy` from image processor

- `src/llamafactory/model/patcher.py`
  - Monkey-patches visual forward to inject MTS parameters
  - Initializes MTS processor with config

- `src/llamafactory/model/loader.py`
  - Freezes CLIP text encoder after LoRA initialization

## Key Parameters

- `high_res_scale`: Resolution multiplier for high-res processing (default: 2.0)
- `base_resolution`: Base image resolution (default: 224)
- `text_prompt`: Optional text guidance for visual attention
- `bbox_scale_xy`: Bounding box scaling factors (sy, sx)
- `instruction`: Full instruction text for context

## Usage

```yaml
use_multi_scale: true
scale_layer: 1  # Use Layer 1 features for scale prediction
conf_thresh: 0.5
scale_thresh: 0.6
base_resolution: 112  # Base processing resolution (short side)
high_res_scale: 0.2   # HR scale factor: HR resolution = base_resolution * high_res_scale = 224
```

Dataset JSON should include bounding boxes in `bbox` field.

